{%- comment -%}
Typography overrides. The theme's stylesheet lives inside the al-folio gem, so
it is not edited here; these rules are layered on top from each page instead.

Measured before changing: body was 1rem / 1.5 line-height, and headings carried
no explicit size, so h2 and h4 sat too close to body text to separate sections.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  /* Body copy: a touch larger and more open than the 1rem / 1.5 default. */
  .post article p,
  .post article li {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .post article li {
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  /* The address block under the photo is a caption, not body copy. */
  .post .more-info p {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  /* Section headings, sized to step down clearly from the page title. */
  .post article h2 {
    font-size: 1.55rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 2.4rem 0 0.8rem;
  }
  .post article h4 {
    font-size: 1.16rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 1.9rem 0 0.55rem;
  }

  /* The theme bolds the given name only, which reads as a mistake rather than
     as a device. One weight for the whole name. */
  .post-title,
  .post-title .font-weight-bold {
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .post-header .desc {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  /* Publication numbers. The theme renders `abbr` as a filled pill, which was
     right for a venue label and wrong for a running number. Plain digits. */
  .publications .abbr .badge {
    background: none !important;
    background-color: transparent !important;
    color: #8b929c;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 0;
    width: auto !important;
    text-align: left;
    border-radius: 0;
  }

  /* Equal-contribution note: its own line, set back from the citation. */
  .publications .periodical + .periodical {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: #8b929c;
    margin-top: 0.15rem;
  }
</style>
